NAME
    unset - remove shell variables

SYNOPSIS
    unset NAME...

DESCRIPTION
    Removes each named variable from both the current shell's variable
    table and its exported variable set. Subsequent references to an
    unset variable ($NAME) expand to an empty string.

EXAMPLES
    FOO=bar
    unset FOO
    echo "$FOO"

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    export(1), source(1)
